track_offset = Vector2(0, -225)
info = "Click and drag up or down (or scroll) on SCOPES to zoom in or out. Zooming in allows bodies to be visually acquired sooner."

[node name="tutorialDiscoverPrelude" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_7r03o")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
target_objective_wID = "tutorialDiscoverPrelude"
text_box_size = Vector2(300, 100)
track = NodePath("../../control/tabs_and_ca_scroll/tabs/OVERVIEW/actions_panel")
track_offset = Vector2(0, -300)
info = "[b]The location of Prelude has been added to the SYSTEM LIST. However, it has not yet been discovered.

Discover a body by visually acquiring it. Click on the the triple question mark on the SYSTEM LIST to lock, and then press the 'ORBIT' action in the ACTIONS PANEL.[/b]
[img]res://graphics/system-map/actions-panel/orbit_icon.png[/img]"

[node name="tutorialFollowPrelude" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_7r03o")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
target_objective_wID = "tutorialFollowPrelude"
text_box_size = Vector2(300, 100)
track = NodePath("../../control/tabs_and_ca_scroll/tabs/OVERVIEW")
info = "[i] * An estimated value of 514 nanites has been gleaned from the discovery of Prelude. There is still another way to gain exploration data from it.[/i]

The question mark adjacent to Prelude on the SYSTEM LIST symbolises an undocumented anomaly - these can result in rewards or tragedy. Investigating an anomaly requires interacting with it.

Click on Prelude on the SYSTEM LIST to lock, and then press the 'GO-TO' action in the ACTIONS PANEL. Wormholes, space stations, planetary anomalies, and other phenomena are all interacted with through the 'GO-TO' action.
[img]res://graphics/system-map/actions-panel/go_to_icon.png[/img]"

[node name="tutorialMarkIngress" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_7r03o")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
target_objective_wID = "tutorialMarkIngress"
text_box_size = Vector2(300, 100)
track = NodePath("../../control/scopes_snap_scroll/core_and_value_scroll/core_panel_bg/core_panel_scroll/core_panel/core_margin/core_scroll/barycenter_container")
track_offset = Vector2(0, -350)
info = "[i] * Your data value is maximised by discovering all bodies within a star system. The SYSTEM LIST currently underlines a missing body further than Prelude. [/i]

A wormhole named Ingress is situated in a higher orbit around King.

The BARYCENTER VISUALIZER displays the direction of other bodies from the locked body with a blip. Click on Prelude on the SYSTEM LIST to lock, adjust your LIDAR direction so it matches the direction of the blip which is oscillating (only wormholes oscillate), use a smaller scan arc, and press the 'PING' button. Dark red blips are beyond your current scan arc. Remember to ping three times to mark.
[img=150%x75%]res://graphics/objective/tutorial_barycenter_example.png[/img]"

